    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2428" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănăglyptus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-phus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάγλυπτος</span> or
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φος</span>; in sculpture, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>wrought</i> or <i>carved in bas-relief</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
					Orell. 3838</span></i>.— Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănăglypta</span></b> ,
			ōrum, n., <i>work
				in bas-relief</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 33, 11, 49, § 139</span></i>,
			where the old form was <i>anaglypha.</i></div>
